id: pm-gh1655
title: "GH-1655: SDK placeholder and type refusals name CLI flags, and parent: null is refused, so typed callers have no documented way to clear a field"
description: "Since GH-1614 (pm-gh1614) typed PmClient fields keep CLI sentinels literal. Typed SDK callers now get refusals written for the CLI: create/update parent 'none' says 'Use --unset parent', an empty parent says 'Use --parent none to unset', a self-parent says 'Use --unset parent', a missing strict parent says 'use --parent none', and parent/assignee null fail a string type check (invalid_argument_value) instead of meaning 'no value'. assignee 'none' now stores a person called none with no advisory. Reproduced on 2026.11.3 dist in a sandbox tracker."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1655",refusals,sdk,sentinels
created_at: "2026-11-03T21:19:36.501Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-03T22:35:55.907Z"
assignee: "harness:claude-code"
claim_principal: "harness:claude-code#436e44ca2d204a1ee603915a"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Typed SDK create/update refusals for placeholder, empty and self parent name the SDK remedy (unset: ['parent'] or omit parent) and never a CLI flag, with a spec per refusal; A typed SDK null on a clearable scalar field (parent, assignee, and every field the unset list accepts) clears it exactly like unset: [field]; null on a field that cannot be cleared refuses naming the field, with specs; A typed SDK create/update whose clearable scalar equals a former clear sentinel (none, null, -) succeeds and returns a stable advisory warning naming the field and the unset form; CLI behaviour and wording are unchanged: --parent none still clears, and CLI refusals still name CLI flags, proven by the existing CLI specs; docs/SDK.md documents null-as-clear and the advisory, and the SDK surface snapshot records any type widening"
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
expected_result: "A typed SDK caller that hits a parent refusal is told the SDK form, and null clears a clearable field"
actual_result: "create({parent:'none'}) refuses naming --unset parent; create({parent:null}) refuses 'create parent must be a string.'; create({assignee:'none'}) stores the literal silently"
