comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T21:39:48.919Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented. (1) Caller vocabulary: core/item/literal-mutation-input.ts gains MutationInputAudience, mutationInputAudience (literal-marked typed SDK/MCP input is 'sdk', a CLI adapter's bag is 'cli'), mutationOptionLabel, sdkClearRemedy and emptyMutationOptionMessage. normalizeParentReferenceValue, validateMissingParentReference, assertParentReferenceIsNotSelf and validateSprintOrReleaseValue take an optional audience (default 'cli', so the public advanced exports keep their wording); create/update pass it, and update's empty assignee/closeReason refusals use it. SDK wording: parent must not be the placeholder \"none\". Pass unset: [\"parent\"] or null to clear it, or omit parent. (2) Null clears: foldNullClearsIntoUnset (sdk/lifecycle/shared-unset-fields.ts) rewrites a typed null on any option the command's unset list covers into its unset token, in both client dispatch (runtime-input normalizedActionOptions) and direct domain calls (prepareNativeMutationOptions). author is excluded (attribution, not a stored field) and keeps its by-name refusal, as do non-clearable fields like title. CREATE_/UPDATE_UNSET_FIELD_DEFINITIONS moved into shared-unset-fields.ts so the fold and both commands share one table (also frees update.ts headroom under the 3400 implementation-line cap). (3) Advisory: literalSentinelAdvisories emits literal_sentinel_stored:<field>:<value> when typed input stores none/null/- in a clearable string field; CLI input never gets it. Probe over 44 fields x 4 tokens (none, -, null, empty) on the rebuilt dist: every parent/sprint/release/assignee/closeReason refusal is SDK-worded; CLI wording verified unchanged in a sandbox (--parent '' / --assignee '' / --sprint '' / --close-reason '' / self parent / strict missing parent)."
